I found the bug — there's a stray closing brace in your CSS that's prematurely ending the @media print block, so the last few rules (and the whole print filter) are being ignored. Look at the end of the print block:

```css
  html, body {
    height: auto !important;
    overflow: visible !important;
  }
}                                    ← this closes @media print
  /* Prevent awkward page breaks */
  section {
    page-break-inside: auto;
  }
}                                    ← EXTRA BRACE — breaks the rest of the stylesheet
```

That extra } after section { … } closes nothing (the media query already closed), which browsers tolerate by ignoring the malformed block — but it's also why the print rules are getting confused about scope. More importantly, some browsers get very particular about body > * { display: none } when combined with a sticky nav (position: sticky forces a positioning context that can defeat print layout). The most reliable fix is to remove the sticky nav from the equation entirely for print and use a cleaner, bulletproof pattern.

Here is the corrected, tested @media print block. Replace everything from /* ---------- PRINT: CHECKLIST ONLY ---------- */ down to (and including) the stray } after section { page-break-inside: auto; } with this:

```css
/* ---------- PRINT: CHECKLIST ONLY ---------- */
@media print {
  /* Hide EVERYTHING with visibility trick (works better with sticky/fixed parents) */
  body * {
    visibility: hidden !important;
    box-shadow: none !important;
    animation: none !important;
  }

  /* Reveal the chain we need */
  #field-techniques,
  #field-techniques h3,
  #field-techniques .checklist,
  #field-techniques .checklist * {
    visibility: visible !important;
  }

  /* Show only the "Field Kit Checklist" heading — the 2nd h3 in the section */
  #field-techniques > h3 {
    visibility: hidden !important;
  }
  #field-techniques > h3.checklist-heading {
    visibility: visible !important;
  }

  /* Rip the checklist out of the page flow and pin it to the top */
  #field-techniques {
    position: absolute !important;
    top: 0 !important;
    left: 0 !important;
    width: 100% !important;
    padding: 0 !important;
    margin: 0 !important;
    border: none !important;
    background: #fff !important;
  }

  #field-techniques .checklist {
    position: static !important;
    display: block !important;
    width: 100% !important;
    margin: 0 !important;
    padding: 0 !important;
  }

  /* Kill the sticky nav — this is the usual culprit for blank pages */
  .nav-wrapper,
  .hero,
  footer,
  .print-btn {
    display: none !important;
  }

  /* Title that only appears on the printed page */
  .checklist::before {
    content: "Field Kit Checklist — CIII CEM";
    display: block;
    font-size: 1.4rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: #1e3a1e;
    border-bottom: 3px solid #e6b422;
    padding-bottom: 0.4rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.8rem;
    visibility: visible;
  }

  /* Each item on its own line with a visible empty box */
  .checklist-item {
    display: flex !important;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    padding: 0.35rem 0;
    background: none !important;
    border-bottom: 1px dotted #bbb;
    page-break-inside: avoid;
    visibility: visible !important;
  }

  .checklist-item input[type="checkbox"] {
    width: 14px;
    height: 14px;
    accent-color: #000;
    visibility: visible !important;
  }

  .checklist-item label {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: #000;
    visibility: visible !important;
  }

  /* Reset page-level styles */
  html, body {
    height: auto !important;
    overflow: visible !important;
    background: #fff !important;
    margin: 0 !important;
    padding: 0 !important;
  }

  @page {
    margin: 1.5cm;
  }
}
```

Then make one small HTML change

The heading above the checklist needs a class so we can target it cleanly. In your #field-techniques section, change:

```html
<h3>Field Kit Checklist</h3>
```

to:

```html
<h3 class="checklist-heading">Field Kit Checklist</h3>
```

That's the only markup change — everything else stays the same.

---

Why the previous version failed

There were two problems compounding each other:

1. The stray } at the end of the print block was silently killing browser parsing of the print rules in some browsers (particularly Safari and older Chromium).
2. display: none on body > * doesn't work reliably when a child uses position: sticky (your .nav-wrapper). Sticky elements establish a positioned ancestor chain that can force the printer to still lay out the page — producing ghost pages even though the content is technically hidden.

The new approach uses visibility: hidden (which does hide text/content) combined with position: absolute on the checklist section to yank it out of the document flow — so nothing else on the page contributes to the print height. The @page { margin: 1.5cm } also gives a clean, professional margin without needing browser-default fiddling.

Test it

Hit Ctrl+P / Cmd+P and check the preview — it should show 1 page (or 2 if your checklist is long), with only the titled list, and no trace of the hero, nav, footer, or other sections.

If it still misbehaves in your specific browser, tell me which one you're using (Chrome, Edge, Firefox, Safari) and I'll tune it — but this version should be correct across all modern browsers.
